records.requirements:
Eligible uses generally include:

Purchasing agricultural conservation easements;
Purchasing development rights;
Paying a landowner for permanently restricting development;
Leveraging local, federal, nonprofit, or private conservation funding;
Completing appraisals;
Conducting surveys;
Performing title searches and title-curative work;
Preparing baseline documentation;
Paying reasonable closing and recordation expenses; and
Other transaction costs specifically authorised by the state award and local program.

records.strategies:
This program does not provide a conventional grant or cost-share payment. It allows a person or entity to obtain DEQ certification for quantified nitrogen or phosphorus reductions generated through an approved nonpoint-source project. Certified credits may then potentially be sold or transferred for use by regulated permittees or development projects, subject to Virginia nutrient-trading laws and geographic-use restrictions.  Conversion of cropland to forest;
Conversion of cropland to permanent grassland;
Conversion of pasture to forest;
Afforestation or reforestation;
Natural forest succession;
Riparian forest buffers;
Wetland restoration or creation;
Stream restoration;
Agricultural nutrient-management improvements;
Certain agricultural BMPs;
Urban stormwater retrofits;
Septic-system upgrades or connections;
Nutrient-removal technologies
